# Kavacha patch 0052 — markdown rendering in workspace notes
# (REMAINING_WORK.md §3 "Workspaces / identity").
#
# Patch 0008 shipped notes as a plain autosaving textarea. People write notes
# in markdown whether or not anything renders it, so the choice was never
# "markdown or not" — it was "rendered or left as punctuation".
#
# WHAT: a Preview toggle in the notes panel header. The textarea remains the
# single source of truth and the thing that autosaves; the preview is a sibling
# shown in its place, never an editable rendering, so there is no DOM-back-to-
# markdown round trip that could rewrite what the user typed. The toggle resets
# to edit on close: this is a notes FIELD, and reopening into a read-only view
# because of a toggle flipped days ago reads as the textarea having vanished.
#
# SECURITY, which is why the renderer is a new module rather than three lines
# of innerHTML: the notes panel is CHROME, not a content document. Assigning
# note text to innerHTML would make "I pasted a snippet into my notes" script
# execution with system privileges. KavachaMarkdown therefore only ever calls
# createElement/createTextNode — there is no HTML parse step at all, so there
# is no sanitiser to get wrong, and raw HTML in a note renders as the literal
# characters typed (which is also the right behaviour for a notes field).
# Link hrefs are separately restricted to http/https/mailto, so
# `[x](javascript:…)` cannot become a clickable javascript: URI; it stays text
# rather than being silently dropped, because the user should see what they
# wrote. Recursion is depth-capped (blockquotes 8, inlines 12): the input is a
# field anyone can paste into, and `"> ".repeat(2000)` is otherwise 2000 levels
# of recursion and 2000 levels of DOM for one pasted line — found by testing,
# not by review.
#
# The renderer is a pure function of (markdown, document) and touches no
# globals, specifically so it can be unit-tested outside a browser. 36 cases
# cover the grammar, the two security invariants and the pathological inputs.
#
# Why a patch: the panel lives in Zen's popupset, the toggle handler is a
# method on nsZenWorkspaces, and the module needs a moz.build entry to resolve
# as resource:///modules/.
#
# Touches: src/zen/common/sys/KavachaMarkdown.sys.mjs (new),
#          src/zen/common/moz.build (register it),
#          src/zen/common/styles/kavacha-notes.inc.css (new) + zen-theme.css,
#          src/browser/base/content/zen-panels/popups.inc (toggle + preview),
#          src/zen/spaces/ZenSpaceManager.mjs (wiring),
#          locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-workspaces.ftl (strings).
# Applies on top of 0051.
